Z||000000||Vlad||09-01-2001||03:45 AM||||Hello guys,<P>I was going to remove control arms today to change ball joints. Everything was fine until I run into problem which I can't solve.<P>The nuts from both ball joints came out without any problem, however, there is no way I can get ball joint bolts out of the knuckle. <BR>I tried fork, hummer and WD-40, but no luck.<BR>I'm sorta stuck now because the suspention is partly disassembled. <BR>What can I do to get them out of the knuckles?<BR>And I'm afraid to think about contlor arms removal already.......<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Primaris||09-01-2001||04:12 AM||||Use a Ball Joint press.  You can get one for free from AutoZone.  They put a charge on a credit card and when you return it refund you.<P>------------------<BR>Signatures are a waste of bandwidth!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||09-01-2001||06:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Vlad:<BR><B>Hello guys,<P>I was going to remove control arms today to change ball joints. Everything was fine until I run into problem which I can't solve.<P>The nuts from both ball joints came out without any problem, however, there is no way I can get ball joint bolts out of the knuckle. <BR>I tried fork, hummer and WD-40, but no luck.<BR>I'm sorta stuck now because the suspention is partly disassembled. <BR>What can I do to get them out of the knuckles?<BR>And I'm afraid to think about contlor arms removal already.......<P>Thanks.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Vlad!<BR>  I just did my front end this week, and I used a fork and 5 lb. hammer...<BR>Just have to whack the fork good and solid!<BR>If you run into problems with the bushings, use a propane torch and burn out the rubber (keep a spray bottle of water handy, and wear safty glasses), then you will see the sleeve on the bolt...<BR>The sleeve is a split tube which can be loosened by inserting increasingly larger screw drivers in the split, and spraying penatrating oil (I like Blaster) in the split...<BR>I only had to do the front lower bushing on each side, as the others came loose easily...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/page1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||09-01-2001||10:34 AM||||Rodney Dickman sells a balljoint separator -- not too expensive, and it works.<P>Sorry, I know that doesn't help you today.<BR>||||reg||1
